  description: Ununennium, also known as eka-francium or simply element 119, is the
    hypothetical chemical element with symbol Uue and atomic number 119. Ununennium
    and Uue are the temporary systematic IUPAC name and symbol respectively, until
    a permanent name is decided upon. In the periodic table of the elements, it is
    expected to be an s-block element, an alkali metal, and the first element in
    the eighth period.
